outputs.L1:
The invention relates to a homogeneous, solid, particulate composition based on urea ammonium sulphate, comprising urea ammonium sulphate together with a urease inhibitor of the phosphoric triamide type, wherein said urea ammonium sulphate-based composition is further characterized in that one or more of the following criteria applies:

a) it contains 5 weight % or less, relative to the total weight of the composition, of one or more alkaline or alkaline-forming inorganic or organic compounds capable of interacting with ammonium sulphate;

b) the urease inhibitor of the phosphoric triamide type is present in a solid, particulate form;

c) an anticaking and/or moisture-repellent coating is applied to the urea ammonium sulphate particulate material.

The composition according to the invention exhibits enhanced properties for reducing ammonia loss arising from urease activity in the soil, and is particularly suitable for use as a fertilizer.

The invention further relates to a method for the manufacture of a homogeneous, solid, particulate composition based on urea ammonium sulphate, comprising urea, ammonium sulphate, and a urease inhibitor of the phosphoric triamide type, in particular N-(n-butyl) thiophosphoric triamide (nBTPT). The invention additionally pertains to a composition or kit of parts comprising:

a) one or more alkaline or alkaline-forming inorganic compounds capable of interacting with ammonium sulphate;

b) the urease inhibitor of the phosphoric triamide type in solid, particulate or liquid form, preferably wherein the urease inhibitor is N-(n-butyl) thiophosphoric triamide (nBTPT);

c) optionally, one or more anticaking and/or moisture-repellent compounds.

outputs.L2:
This invention concerns a uniform, solid, granular composition built around urea ammonium sulphate, containing both urea ammonium sulphate and a phosphoric triamide-class urease inhibitor. This urea ammonium sulphate-based composition is additionally distinguished by satisfying at least one of the following conditions:

a) It contains no more than 5 weight percent, measured against the composition's total weight, of one or several alkaline or alkaline-generating inorganic or organic substances capable of reacting with ammonium sulphate;

b) The phosphoric triamide-type urease inhibitor exists in a solid, granular state;

c) A coating that prevents caking and/or repels moisture is applied to the granular urea ammonium sulphate material.

The composition described here offers enhanced capabilities for limiting the release of ammonia caused by urease activity within soil, making it particularly well-suited for use as a fertilizer.

The invention additionally covers a process for producing a uniform, solid, granular composition based on urea ammonium sulphate, which incorporates urea, ammonium sulphate, and a urease inhibitor belonging to the phosphoric triamide class—specifically N-(n-butyl) thiophosphoric triamide (nBTPT). It further encompasses a composition or kit of parts made up of:

a) one or more alkaline or alkaline-generating inorganic substances able to react with ammonium sulphate;

b) the phosphoric triamide-type urease inhibitor, provided either in solid granular or liquid form, with N-(n-butyl) thiophosphoric triamide (nBTPT) being the preferred inhibitor;

c) optionally, one or more substances that resist caking and/or repel moisture.
